#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wave 40: Just Teens, a Second Time — the floor, exactly.

Wave 39 opened the teen band; this wave's fresh audit measured
it again before anything was built. Per-age coverage at wave
39's close: 3: 160, 4: 160, 5: 329, 6: 426, 7: 496, 8: 530,
9: 524, 10: 518, 11: 456, 12: 446, 13: 88, 14: 88 — ages 13
and 14 are still the thinnest band in the vault by a wide
margin. Inside the band, the primary-category cells measure
seasons 3, outdoor 3, pe-movement 4, music-rhythm 6,
rainy-day 6, icebreakers 7, crafts 7, holidays 9, stem 9,
quiet-focus 15, team-community 19 — a floor of 3.

The gap this wave closes is sized from those cells, exactly:
raising every cell in the band to at least 6 — the level of
the band's own next shelf (music-rhythm, rainy-day) — costs
seasons +3, outdoor +3, pe-movement +2. Eight records. Not a
familiar twelve padded out, and not a token gesture at the
72-wide total gap to the young-end parity figure, which no
single wave could honestly close. Result, asserted in the
wave log: total 715 -> 723; age-13 coverage 88 -> 96 and
age-14 coverage 88 -> 96, every other age unchanged; the
13/14 primary floor rises 3 -> 6; 13-14-only records 12 ->
20; and eight honest picks meet the build validator's 8-12
collection rule at its minimum, so the 29th collection —
"Just Teens, a Second Time" — unlocks with no padding and
no lowered bar.

Deliberate neighbours, kept on purpose and named here:
- compost-heap-temperature-ledger: no compost record exists
  anywhere on the shelf (checked); a heap built, layered,
  turned on a rota and read by thermometer across a season
  is new ground entire.
- first-frost-forecast-desk vs frost-observation (6-12,
  magnifying frost crystals after the fact) and
  weather-journal (7-12, a week of sky-watching): the desk
  works BEFORE the frost — instruments read in the evening,
  a signed forecast issued to real gardeners, and a morning
  verification that grades the forecast, not the weather.
- summer-glut-preserving-day: no preserving or kitchen
  record exists on the shelf (checked); the glut, the jars
  and the one tested recipe followed exactly are new.
- trail-crew-first-pass vs chalk-arrow-trail (3-6, a chalk
  game to follow) and litter-tally-cleanup (a tally walk):
  the crew MAINTAINS a real path — drainage, waymarks by
  permission, a work log — stewardship, not a game or a
  one-off tidy.
- star-party-hosts vs marshmallow-constellations (7-12, an
  indoor craft with sweets): the party hosts a real sky for
  real guests — rehearsed tour, red-light discipline, and
  stories told as stories under the things themselves.
- stream-watch-testing-round: no water-testing record
  exists on the shelf (checked); temperature, clarity and
  invertebrate evidence gathered at a real stream bank is
  new ground entire.
- circuit-course-design-and-coach vs dice-fitness-roll
  (5-12, chance deals the moves): the circuit is DESIGNED —
  stations proposed, tested on the designers, cut or kept
  by evidence, then coached to peers.
- new-game-playtest-league vs board-game-prototype (a
  tabletop game built on a table) and
  upcycle-invention-challenge (objects invented from
  recycling): the league invents games played on feet —
  written rules, stranger playtests, revisions, and a
  league table that rewards clarity over cleverness.

Two drafted records were cut before the pack ran, on the
standing near-dupe discipline: a teen phenology wheel for
the seasons slot — seasonal-rounds-phenology-wheel already
builds that wheel at 7-12, and older annotations do not
make it a new record — and a compass scavenger hunt for
the outdoor slot — compass-course-three-flags (wave 39)
already runs bearings to flags and indoor-scavenger-hunt
already runs the hunt; bolting them together is the same
two games, not a third. Both slots were rebuilt from
genuinely empty ground: no compost record and no trail
maintenance record existed anywhere on the shelf.

The drama/coding lane, recorded not padded (standing rule):
still no drama or coding category among the eleven, and no
validator tag names one. This wave does not invent a
twelfth category either. The lane stays an honest named
gap, and this wave is not briefed to build it.

Safety notes are practical only — no medical claims anywhere.

Run once: dedupes by id, writes data/activities.json and
data/collections.json. Run scripts/build.py afterwards.
"""
